            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Life of Eratosthenes</strong><br>\nEratosthenes was born around 276 BCE in Cyrene, which is now present-day Libya. From a young age, he showed an interest in learning and was educated in Athens. His thirst for knowledge spanned various subjects, reflecting the broad curriculum he would have studied in the vibrant intellectual atmosphere of ancient Greece. He became known for his work in mathematics, geography, and astronomy.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Eratosthenes's Measurement of the Earth</strong><br>\nEratosthenes is most famous for calculating the circumference of the Earth. He used observations of the sun's angle at noon in different cities to make his calculations. On the summer solstice, at local noon, he observed the angle of the sun's shadow in Syene and Alexandria. By using the difference in shadow angles and the distance between the two cities, he estimated the Earth's circumference with remarkable accuracy.</p>\n\n<p><strong>The Sieve of Eratosthenes</strong><br>\nIn mathematics, Eratosthenes is remembered for inventing the \"Sieve of Eratosthenes,\" a method to identify prime numbers. His technique involved listing all numbers up to a desired limit and progressively removing the multiples of each prime number starting from 2. The numbers that were not removed were the prime numbers, which has helped generations understand prime numbers better.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
